{
  "summary": "Settings currently persist on PUT and restart UDP listener in place; no engine selector or general process restart route exists. Graceful shutdown has signal-only ingress stop/recorder flush, while Windows update supplies only external installer-driven relaunch.",
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "apps/backend/src/runtime/boot.ts:131-176",
      "description": "Starts HTTP first, launches historical async backfills without awaiting, registers signal shutdown, starts UDP asynchronously, then sync/stale jobs, native supervisor, tray, maintenance, ready log. UDP precedence: options → RACEIQ_DEV_UDP_PORT → settings → UDP_PORT → 5301."
    },
    {
      "path": "apps/backend/src/runtime/shutdown.ts:1-29",
      "description": "SIGINT/SIGTERM call `gracefulShutdown`: stop compressor; await UDP stop and native supervisor stop concurrently with allSettled; then await `flushSessionRecorder`; finally process.exit(0). No DB/reconcile drain barrier, shared transition state, update hook, or idempotency guard."
    },
    {
      "path": "apps/backend/src/routes/settings-routes.ts:47-71,73-110,244-286",
      "description": "GET `/api/status` reports UDP counters/client count/detected game/current session only. GET `/api/settings` returns saved settings plus live UDP port and secret-presence booleans. PUT parses `PartialSettingsSchema`, merges explicit keys, restarts UDP in-place only on port change, updates WebSocket refresh/cache/login settings, persists, broadcasts onboarding notification; returns merged settings."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/runtime/config/settings.ts:15-64,133-175",
      "description": "`AppSettingsSchema` / `AppSettings` persists ordinary settings; no recorder/engine selection property. `PartialSettingsSchema` is schema partial. `saveSettings` validates and atomically renames settings JSON."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/runtime/update/check.ts:232-317",
      "description": "`applyUpdate` downloads/checks installer while running, broadcasts progress, spawns detached installer; schedules process.exit(0) after 500ms. Does not call app shutdown or await capture/database drain itself."
    },
    {
      "path": "apps/backend/src/routes/system/update-routes.ts:17-25",
      "description": "POST `/api/update/apply` awaits `applyUpdate`; documents then restart, relays errors as 400."
    },
    {
      "path": "client/src/components/settings/connection/ConnectionSection.tsx:1-89",
      "description": "Connection UI owns UDP-port local input/save state; `useSaveSettings().mutateAsync({udpPort})`; no engine selector/restart handling. Rest is connection guide and refresh/render preferences."
    },
    {
      "path": "client/src/stores/telemetry.ts:9-76,89-155,172-203",
      "description": "Frontend `DisplaySettings` mirrors user-facing settings (cacheMaxMB included) and optional API-injected fields. `ServerStatus` contains UDP/live game/session fields, no recorder status/engine. Telemetry store owns transient live telemetry view/status and update progress, not persistent replay packet cache."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/runtime/README.md:21-30",
      "description": "Runtime notes existing restart semantics: UDP listener restart replaces status/flush loops; signal shutdown ordering described as compressor then settle recorder/native stops before exit. Existing update/lifecycle focused suites named."
    },
    {
      "path": "client/src/components/UpdateModal.tsx:21-23",
      "description": "Existing update progress vocabulary includes downloading/installing/reconnecting/complete."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/runtime/telemetry/cache.ts",
      "description": "[INFERENCE] Parsed per-lap telemetry LRU owns replay/analysis cache; settings comment and route call `setCacheMaxBytes`; telemetry Zustand store only owns live presentation state."
    }
  ],
  "architecture": "No global process restart mechanism found in inspected exact searches. Existing restarts are UDP socket replacement and Windows update installer relaunch. Bun remains implicit sole engine. Recommendation: persist engine choice as a settings field (`bun` default, `rust` opt-in), expose selected and active separately in status; PUT changing selection persists desired value and returns explicit restart-required state, not silently hot-switching. Restart must be an explicit drain-then-exit/relaunch capability owned by launcher; absent launcher means process must not claim restart completed. Preserve current Bun behavior/default.",
  "report": "**Shutdown/drain contract.** Current signal path stops compressor, stops UDP/native ingress concurrently, then waits for session recorder flush, then exits. `flushSessionRecorder` is recorder/file barrier only; no explicit pending DB/event callback or race-result reconciliation barrier is awaited. `bootServer` starts `backfillAllRaceResults()` and LMU identity backfill detached from startup and does not retain their promises for shutdown. Thus required capture→DB/reconcile drain is not currently established. UDP settings restart is listener-local (`udpListener.restart`→`stop` then start), not process restart and not proof of capture/DB barrier.\n\n**Process restart evidence.** Exact search over `apps/backend/src;server/runtime;packages/tooling-b…
}

